---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Kadanco. Your marketing function, owned and executed."
  description="Kadanco is a senior, full-stack marketing function for B2B companies. Two operators own the strategy and run the execution. €100M+ in pipeline generated, 12+ vendors replaced per client, results in 2 weeks. No agency overhead, no juniors, no freelancer juggling."
>
  <!-- NAV -->
  <header class="nav">
    <div class="container nav-inner">
      <!-- LOGO PLACEHOLDER: replace the wordmark with your final asset -->
      <a class="brandmark" href="#top" aria-label="Kadanco — home">Kadanco</a>
      <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary">
        <a class="navlink" href="#approach">Approach</a>
        <a class="navlink" href="#capabilities">Capabilities</a>
        <a class="navlink" href="#use-cases">Use cases</a>
        <a class="navlink" href="#founders">Who we are</a>
        <button class="btn btn-accent" data-open-modal>Let's talk</button>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="top">

    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="section hero">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">A senior marketing function for B2B companies</span>
        <div class="hero-head">
          <h1>Your marketing function. <span class="hl">Owned and executed.</span></h1>
          <svg class="bars" width="76" height="48" viewBox="0 0 76 48" aria-hidden="true">
            <rect x="0" y="27" width="13" height="21" rx="3" fill="#1A8B8B" />
            <rect x="21" y="18" width="13" height="30" rx="3" fill="#A6B00F" />
            <rect x="42" y="9" width="13" height="39" rx="3" fill="#E96225" />
            <rect x="63" y="0" width="13" height="48" rx="3" fill="#050A30" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="lead">
          Kadanco is a complete marketing function for B2B companies. Two senior operators take
          ownership of the strategy and run the execution themselves. One team, one system of action,
          one number you control. No agency overhead, no junior hand-offs, no stack of freelancers to manage.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <button class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-open-modal>Let's talk</button>
          <a class="btn btn-outline btn-lg" href="#capabilities">See the system</a>
        </div>

        <!-- facts strip -->
        <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:42px;margin-bottom:0">What the founders have delivered</p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat stat-1"><div class="stat-num">€100M+</div><div class="stat-label">pipeline generated for clients</div></div>
          <div class="stat stat-2"><div class="stat-num">12+</div><div class="stat-label">vendors replaced per client</div></div>
          <div class="stat stat-3"><div class="stat-num">2 weeks</div><div class="stat-label">to first results</div></div>
          <div class="stat stat-4"><div class="stat-num">15+ yrs</div><div class="stat-label">operating experience each</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CAPABILITY STRIP -->
    <section class="section-tight">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow e-teal">The whole stack, one team</span>
        <div class="cap-strip">
          Positioning &middot; ABM &amp; outbound &middot; Demand gen &middot; Content &amp; ghostwriting &middot; SEO &amp; GEO &middot; Paid &middot; Brand &amp; web &middot; Events &middot; CRO &middot; RevOps &amp; automation &middot; Partnerships &middot; Lifecycle
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PROBLEM -->
    <section class="section section-tight">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow e-orange">The overhead problem</span>
        <h2>Most marketing spend buys management, not execution.</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="max-width:64ch;margin-top:14px">
          At EUR 2 to 5M you need a full marketing function. Every standard way of getting one taxes
          you somewhere: in overhead, in ownership, or in time.
        </p>
        <div class="grid cols-2" style="margin-top:36px">
          <div class="card pain pain-teal">
            <h3>Agencies sell senior, staff junior.</h3>
            <p>You pay partner rates and get work the interns are learning on, wrapped in an account-management layer that adds cost and removes ownership.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card pain pain-orange">
            <h3>A fractional CMO writes the plan, then leaves you to run it.</h3>
            <p>Strategy without execution is a slide deck. Someone still has to do the work, and that someone is you.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card pain pain-citron">
            <h3>Imported playbooks stall.</h3>
            <p>Tactics that worked elsewhere get run unchanged and underperform. The market, the language and the channels get treated as an afterthought.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card pain pain-navy">
            <h3>Twelve tools and five freelancers, no owner.</h3>
            <p>Everyone runs a slice, nobody owns the funnel, and the coordination overhead lands on your desk. The numbers never reconcile.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- APPROACH -->
    <section id="approach" class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow e-teal">How we operate</span>
        <h2>We don't advise the work. We own it and execute it.</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="max-width:64ch;margin-top:16px">
          Kadanco operates as your marketing function, not a vendor attached to it. The two people who
          scope the work are the two people who do it. We take ownership of the outcome, run the motions
          ourselves, and keep the whole system pointed at pipeline. Four clients at a time, so every
          account gets senior execution.
        </p>
        <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:38px">
          <div class="card edge-teal">
            <span class="tag tag-teal">One owner</span>
            <h3 style="margin:14px 0 8px">One team, accountable for everything.</h3>
            <p>A single team owns the whole function and one number, not a roster of specialists you have to coordinate.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card edge-orange">
            <span class="tag tag-orange">Senior execution</span>
            <h3 style="margin:14px 0 8px">The strategists do the work.</h3>
            <p>The operators who set the direction do the hands-on work. No junior delivery, no account layer, no markup.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card edge-citron">
            <span class="tag tag-citron">One system of action</span>
            <h3 style="margin:14px 0 8px">Twelve motions, one engine.</h3>
            <p>Every motion runs as part of one connected system, so the whole stack compounds instead of leaking between vendors.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CAPABILITIES -->
    <section id="capabilities" class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">The system</span>
        <h2>One function. The whole stack.</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="max-width:64ch;margin-top:16px">
          Twelve capabilities, run as one connected system of action. We don't sell them a la carte.
          We take ownership of the function and deploy whichever motions move your pipeline.
        </p>
        <div class="grid cols-2" style="margin-top:38px">
          <div class="card edge-teal">
            <span class="tag tag-teal">Pipeline &amp; demand</span>
            <ul class="svc-list">
              <li><strong>ABM &amp; outbound</strong><span>Targeted account motion into the buyers you actually want.</span></li>
              <li><strong>Paid</strong><span>Google, LinkedIn and Meta, run with ABM-level targeting.</span></li>
              <li><strong>Events</strong><span>Rooms worth being in: scored, built, filled, and worked for pipeline.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card edge-orange">
            <span class="tag tag-orange">Brand &amp; content</span>
            <ul class="svc-list">
              <li><strong>Brand &amp; website</strong><span>Identity, design and build that read as the category leader.</span></li>
              <li><strong>Content &amp; ghostwriting</strong><span>A consistent publishing motion in your team's voice.</span></li>
              <li><strong>Creative &amp; sales collateral</strong><span>Decks, one-pagers and video the sales team actually uses.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card edge-citron">
            <span class="tag tag-citron">Positioning &amp; strategy</span>
            <ul class="svc-list">
              <li><strong>Messaging &amp; positioning</strong><span>Sharper words and a category you can own.</span></li>
              <li><strong>Growth strategy</strong><span>GTM and quarterly operating plans you can act on Monday.</span></li>
              <li><strong>Partnerships</strong><span>Co-marketing, integrations and channel that compound.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card edge-navy">
            <span class="tag">Engine &amp; ops</span>
            <ul class="svc-list">
              <li><strong>SEO &amp; GEO</strong><span>Rank on publish, and get cited by AI search.</span></li>
              <li><strong>CRO</strong><span>Find the leaks, run the experiments, lift the rate.</span></li>
              <li><strong>RevOps &amp; automation</strong><span>CRM, lifecycle and attribution that finally reconcile.</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- USE CASES -->
    <section id="use-cases" class="section band-pink">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow e-navy">Use cases</span>
        <h2>What the function delivers.</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="max-width:64ch;margin-top:16px">
          A few of the outcomes teams hire us for, and the bundle of motions behind each. This is how
          the engine runs, not a menu.
        </p>
        <div class="grid cols-2" style="margin-top:38px">
          <div class="card edge-teal">
            <span class="tag tag-teal">Founder-led content &amp; pipeline</span>
            <p style="margin-top:14px"><strong>Situation.</strong> The founder's insight is the company's best asset and it is trapped in their head.</p>
            <p><strong>The bundle.</strong> Messaging &amp; positioning, ghostwriting &amp; content, SEO &amp; GEO, outbound warmed by the content, and RevOps to track what converts.</p>
            <p><strong>What you own.</strong> A consistent publishing motion in the founder's voice, feeding measurable pipeline instead of vanity engagement.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card edge-orange">
            <span class="tag tag-orange">Rebuild that lifts conversion</span>
            <p style="margin-top:14px"><strong>Situation.</strong> The product moved on, the brand and site didn't, and the funnel leaks.</p>
            <p><strong>The bundle.</strong> Positioning, brand &amp; website rebuild, sales collateral, CRO, and lifecycle &amp; automation.</p>
            <p><strong>What you own.</strong> A site and message that match where the company actually is, plus an instrumented funnel you keep improving.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card edge-citron">
            <span class="tag tag-citron">DACH market entry</span>
            <p style="margin-top:14px"><strong>Situation.</strong> You have product and traction, but no one owns the German-speaking market in its own language.</p>
            <p><strong>The bundle.</strong> Localised positioning, a German content engine, LinkedIn for the team, an event motion, and distribution.</p>
            <p><strong>What you own.</strong> A German-language presence that compounds weekly, existing assets finally working in-market, and a pipeline motion your salespeople don't run themselves.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card edge-navy">
            <span class="tag">Event pipeline engineering</span>
            <p style="margin-top:14px"><strong>Situation.</strong> Trade shows and conferences eat budget and team time, but the pipeline never gets attributed.</p>
            <p><strong>The bundle.</strong> Events scored by ICP overlap and persona density, LinkedIn and Meta ABM from four weeks out with calendar holds, hosted dinners and roundtables where deals close, plus same-day enrichment, CRM sync and follow-up sequenced by lead type.</p>
            <p><strong>What you own.</strong> Attendees who recognise you before they walk in, meetings booked into a held calendar, and a CFO-grade ROI report inside 30 days with every meeting tagged.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- OPERATING MODEL -->
    <section id="how" class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow e-teal">How we work</span>
        <h2>Kickoff to live execution in 14 days.</h2>
        <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:38px">
          <div class="card step">
            <span class="step-no no-teal">01</span>
            <h3>Map</h3>
            <p>We learn the market, the ICP, the funnel and the numbers, then agree the few motions that move pipeline most.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card step">
            <span class="step-no no-citron">02</span>
            <h3>Own</h3>
            <p>We take the work off your team and run it ourselves: brand, site, campaigns, content, systems. No briefs over a wall.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card step">
            <span class="step-no no-orange">03</span>
            <h3>Compound</h3>
            <p>First execution live inside two weeks. Then we run in quarterly cycles (plan, ship, review) and the system compounds.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="principles">Single point of contact &middot; Monthly prioritisation &middot; One blended rate &middot; Transparent reporting &middot; Results over activity.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHO WE ARE -->
    <section id="founders" class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow e-navy">Who we are</span>
        <h2>Two operators. One owner for the whole function.</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="max-width:66ch;margin-top:16px">
          Kadanco is two senior operators in Berlin, fifteen-plus years each. The people who own your
          account are the people doing the work.
        </p>
        <div class="grid cols-2" style="margin-top:38px">
          <div class="card founder">
            <!-- PHOTO: LinkedIn CDN links expire. Replace src with a self-hosted /public image. -->
            <img src="https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4D03AQEnZ21QpKUzyw/profile-displayphoto-scale_200_200/B4DZq25JOKIEAY-/0/1764005028381?e=1782950400&v=beta&t=dBKuzYs_ZuP9XVARuZB6RXydEXDFbKp1jJWpM9I1D58" alt="Maria" class="avatar" />
            <div>
              <h3>Maria</h3>
              <span class="role">Brand, website &amp; systems</span>
              <p>Product, brand and design systems for B2B software; earlier, design for Opel, Mercedes-Benz, Toyota and Postbank. German, English.</p>
              <!-- TODO: replace # with Maria's LinkedIn URL -->
              <a class="tag tag-teal" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View profile on LinkedIn</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card founder">
            <img src="https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4D03AQH2pg2p6SkR8g/profile-displayphoto-shrink_200_200/profile-displayphoto-shrink_200_200/0/1728300291304?e=1782950400&v=beta&t=if1GJMJbGKpWBggZTHHHOi-qne7HElqPs1fCxLDiSaI" alt="Karan" class="avatar" />
            <div>
              <h3>Karan</h3>
              <span class="role">Growth, GTM &amp; positioning</span>
              <p>Founder of hubsell; advisor to dozens of B2B companies on positioning, demand and content. Dutch, English.</p>
              <a class="tag tag-orange" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/krnshrm/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View profile on LinkedIn</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA BAND -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="on-dark cta-panel">
          <span class="eyebrow e-pink">Let's talk</span>
          <h2>Tell us what you need to move.</h2>
          <p>We'll tell you the motions we'd run and what we'd own. Quarterly engagements, four client slots, senior execution from week one. Reply within 24 hours.</p>
          <button class="btn btn-accent btn-lg" data-open-modal>Start a conversation</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="container footer-inner">
      <span class="brandmark">Kadanco</span>
      <p>Your marketing function, owned and executed. Berlin, Germany.</p>
      <div class="footer-links">
        <a href="mailto:hello@kadanco.com">hello@kadanco.com</a>
        <a href="#" aria-label="Kadanco on LinkedIn">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="/imprint/">Imprint &amp; Privacy</a>
      </div>
      <p class="small">© 2026 Kadanco UG</p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <!-- ============================================================
       PLUNK: contact modal + script.
       This posts to /api/contact, where your Plunk Cloudflare function lives.
       If your live form is wired differently (different endpoint or fields),
       REPLACE THIS WHOLE BLOCK (modal + script) with your current one.
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="modal-overlay" id="contact" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <div class="modal">
      <button class="x" data-close-modal aria-label="Close dialog">✕</button>
      <div id="form-body">
        <span class="eyebrow">Let's talk</span>
        <h3 id="contact-title">Start a conversation</h3>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:6px">Tell us a bit about you and we'll reply within 24 hours.</p>
        <form id="contact-form" novalidate>
          <!-- Honeypot: hidden from people, catches bots. Leave empty. -->
          <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
            <label for="f-hp">Leave this field empty</label>
            <input id="f-hp" name="_gotcha" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
          <div class="field"><label for="f-name">Name</label><input id="f-name" name="name" autocomplete="name" required /></div>
          <div class="field"><label for="f-email">Work email</label><input id="f-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required /></div>
          <div class="field"><label for="f-company">Company</label><input id="f-company" name="company" autocomplete="organization" /></div>
          <div class="field"><label for="f-website">Website <span class="muted">(optional)</span></label><input id="f-website" name="website" /></div>
          <div class="field"><label for="f-goal">What are you trying to grow?</label><textarea id="f-goal" name="goal"></textarea></div>
          <p class="form-error" id="form-error" role="alert" style="display:none"></p>
          <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Send</button>
        </form>
      </div>
      <div id="form-success" class="success" style="display:none">
        <div class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</div>
        <h3>Thanks — talk soon.</h3>
        <p class="muted" style="margin-top:6px">We'll be in touch within 24 hours.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var overlay = document.getElementById('contact');
      var lastFocus = null;
      function openModal() {
        lastFocus = document.activeElement;
        overlay.classList.add('open');
        document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
        var first = overlay.querySelector('input, button');
        if (first) first.focus();
      }
      function closeModal() {
        overlay.classList.remove('open');
        document.body.style.overflow = '';
        if (lastFocus && lastFocus.focus) lastFocus.focus();
      }
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-open-modal]').forEach(function (b) {
        b.addEventListener('click', function (e) { e.preventDefault(); openModal(); });
      });
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-close-modal]').forEach(function (b) {
        b.addEventListener('click', closeModal);
      });
      overlay.addEventListener('click', function (e) { if (e.target === overlay) closeModal(); });
      document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
        if (e.key === 'Escape' && overlay.classList.contains('open')) closeModal();
      });
      var form = document.getElementById('contact-form');
      var errEl = document.getElementById('form-error');
      function val(id) { var el = document.getElementById(id); return el ? el.value : ''; }
      form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        if (!form.checkValidity()) { form.reportValidity(); return; }
        var btn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
        var label = btn.textContent;
        btn.disabled = true; btn.textContent = 'Sending…';
        errEl.style.display = 'none';
        fetch('/api/contact', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({
            name: val('f-name'), email: val('f-email'), company: val('f-company'),
            website: val('f-website'), goal: val('f-goal'), _gotcha: val('f-hp')
          })
        }).then(function (res) {
          return res.json().catch(function () { return {}; }).then(function (out) {
            if (res.ok && out.ok) {
              document.getElementById('form-body').style.display = 'none';
              document.getElementById('form-success').style.display = 'block';
            } else {
              throw new Error((out && out.error) || 'Something went wrong.');
            }
          });
        }).catch(function (err) {
          errEl.textContent = err.message + ' You can also email hello@kadanco.com.';
          errEl.style.display = 'block';
          btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = label;
        });
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Layout>